      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walnut_Grove%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The various tongs provided support and protection to newly arriving Chinese immigrants and were in constant competition for influence within Walnut Grove’s Chinatown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walnut_Grove%2C_California",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Walnut Grove is one of the only remaining Japanese-American built cities in the United States, a National Historic Landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
